KG42.register("nodes-5ab8bc0d6fb6562c45dae96d",{"id":"COMP-20e312b579d3a493","code":"PRC017","label":"Piecewise supply-demand-ratio purchase and sale pricing with trading-side applicability","definition":"Contains SDR internal electricity price formation and transaction-side applicable definitions. The pricing constraint specifies: when 0≤SDR^h≤1, Pr_sell^h=(λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^h+λ^{sell}), Pr_buy^h=SDR^h·Pr_sell^h+(1−SDR^h)λ^{buy}; when SDR^h>1, both prices are λ^{sell}. When prosumer NP_i^h\u003c0, Pr_sell^h applies; when NP_i^h≥0, Pr_buy^h applies. At trade execution, Pr_buy and Pr_sell are separately defined as the ESP electricity purchase and sale unit prices, respectively; this independent transaction-side specification must be retained.","layer":"L6","template_code":"PGR","concept_id":"pricing.local","concept_ids":["pricing.local"],"identity_dimensions":{"identity_fields":["Object: the internal unit electricity price of the sharing area and the applicable transaction side","Core operation: form electricity prices by SDR segments and select the applicable price according to the sign of the prosumer's net quantity","Output: Pr_sell^h, Pr_buy^h, and Pr_i^h","Independent definition: Pr_buy and Pr_sell, named at the execution point according to the ESP purchase/sale direction"]},"exclusions":["The electricity price boundaries are the feed-in tariff and the grid purchase price.","After receiving the updated net quantity, ESP recalculates the price; when dispatch no longer changes, the final price is determined.","When 0≤SDR≤1, retain the revenue-expenditure constraint TBP·Pr_buy=TSP·Pr_sell+(TBP−TSP)λ^{buy}.","The buying-price formula retains the original formula; no service-fee term is added additionally because of the textual description of the fee composition.","The ESP-side naming and the buy/sell directions of the prosumer net-quantity branch are retained separately."],"members":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The ESP performs price-signal coordination by broadcasting updated internal prices during the iterative interaction with PV prosumers. Scope: Closed-loop iterative demand response within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Local internal prices provide the signal guiding each prosumer's scheduling decisions, with forecast PV power, load consumption and willingness taken into account. Scope: Decentralized scheduling of PV prosumers during iterative energy sharing with demand response. The coordination loop is limited to K iterations. Scope: Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. Stop the price-signal iteration when the specified tolerance condition is satisfied. Scope: Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. Condition: The norm of the difference between the current internal price Pr and the previous internal price Pr_{old} is at most ε.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. | Closed-loop iterative demand response within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Decentralized scheduling of PV prosumers during iterative energy sharing with demand response.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"aa8f1f27d192643963a44e8fa99ed94cbde6970387ed22ac0c02463bcebd36c1","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Organizing energy-sharing exchanges requires a coordinator, instantiated as the Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Scope: Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. The ESP coordinates energy-sharing activities and executes the local trading agency role by purchasing surplus electricity from PV prosumers and selling electricity to other prosumers. Scope: ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone. Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"374605ad1b01a6db8884beca3c6b0faad6a333c662310321d595647cc6a10b0b","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"Updated requested net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h ≥ 0, which contribute to total buying power. Updated offered net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h \u003c 0, whose magnitudes contribute to total selling power. The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. Final internal prices are decided when the price-coordination process reaches a state in which no PV prosumer can adjust its schedule further. Scope: Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. Condition: After sufficient iterations, all PV prosumers can no longer adjust their schedules in response to the internal prices. The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1. Internal prices must remain between the feed-in tariff and the utility-grid electricity purchase price. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Internal-price design must guarantee the economic balance of the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. The internal selling price is Pr^{h}_{sell} = (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}). Scope: Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR^h ≤ 1. Both internal buying and selling prices equal the utility-grid export tariff. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. Condition: SDR > 1. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_sell^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h \u003c 0. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_buy^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h ≥ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C011"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"56caf15ff85b7048a35707f2567847b37f3ebab30e4076668d222d792bbea136","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":true},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h. The service fee is directly proportional to the amount of shared local PV energy. Scope: The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. Each prosumer's service-fee share is allocated according to its contribution of shared local energy. Scope: Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. The service fee should cover sharing-power losses and other possible expenditures for organizing sharing activities. Scope: Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"fe990a393f5f5a128c4aeb63d22e38523e42ffec212540ef5888171d9331c382","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008","node_id":"pricing.local","function":"pricing.local","unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","anchor":false}],"paper_ids":["06-sdr_energy_sharing"],"evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","quote":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"TSP h to SDRh = (7) TBP h th Considering the ﬂuctuation of PV power and users’ load, the λb SDR is a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","quote":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"certain time slot based on the net power. Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power","equation_id":"(4)-(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power (TBP) at time slot h can be calculated as:\nTSP^{h} = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \u003c 0 \\quad (4)\nTBP^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \\geq 0 \\quad (5)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power (TBP) at time slot h can be calculated as:\nTSP^{h} = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \u003c 0 \\quad (4)\nTBP^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \\geq 0 \\quad (5)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"der When SDR = 0, which means no PV prosumer sells power, ded the required energy is bought from the","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34).","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal prices should be bounded between the feed-in tariff and electricity prices of utility grid; ii) as the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional; iii) the economic balance should always be guaranteed for the energy sharing zone.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal prices should be bounded between the feed-in tariff and electricity prices of utility grid; ii) as the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional; iii) the economic balance should always be guaranteed for the energy sharing zone."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function of internal selling price can be formulated as: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR^{h}) = { (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}), 0 ≤ SDR^{h} ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR^{h} > 1 } (30)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function of internal selling price can be formulated as: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR^{h}) = { (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}), 0 ≤ SDR^{h} ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR^{h} > 1 } (30)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p11-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":11,"printed_page":"3579","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"SDR. When SDR > 1, there must be extra PV energy export to the utility grid, then the selling price ","equation_id":"(27)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional. Thus, the price decrease with the higher SDR and increased with the lower SDR. When SDR > 1, there must be extra PV energy export to the utility grid, then the selling price could be set as λsell due to the constraints of feed-in tariff. When 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, as the sharing energy is lower than the load demand of the microgrid, the internal price can be set in accordance with the function of inverse proportion 1/(ax + b). Thus, we can use 1/(ax + b) as the fitting function to obtain the relationship between internal selling price and SDR: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR) = { 1/(aSDR+b), 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR > 1 } (27)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"According to the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional. Thus, the price decrease with the higher SDR and increased with the lower SDR. When SDR > 1, there must be extra PV energy export to the utility grid, then the selling price could be set as λsell due to the constraints of feed-in tariff. When 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, as the sharing energy is lower than the load demand of the microgrid, the internal price can be set in accordance with the function of inverse proportion 1/(ax + b). Thus, we can use 1/(ax + b) as the fitting function to obtain the relationship between internal selling price and SDR: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR) = { 1/(aSDR+b), 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR > 1 } (27)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","quote":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"h=1 where inci is the equivalent inconvenience cost of PV prosumer i, αi is the sensitivity coefﬁcie","equation_id":"(14),(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness.","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34).","paper":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","quote":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}],"candidate_only":true,"classification_subtypes":["internal_tariff_formation_and_application"],"projection_statuses":["composite"],"taxonomy":{"primary_family":"kind-L6-85cb564921","secondary_families":[],"stage":"L6","ontological_kind":"composite_rule"},"semantic_definition":{},"source_units":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","source_occurrences":[{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R002","market_meaning":"The ESP performs price-signal coordination by broadcasting updated internal prices during the iterative interaction with PV prosumers. Scope: Closed-loop iterative demand response within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Local internal prices provide the signal guiding each prosumer's scheduling decisions, with forecast PV power, load consumption and willingness taken into account. Scope: Decentralized scheduling of PV prosumers during iterative energy sharing with demand response. The coordination loop is limited to K iterations. Scope: Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. Stop the price-signal iteration when the specified tolerance condition is satisfied. Scope: Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. Condition: The norm of the difference between the current internal price Pr and the previous internal price Pr_{old} is at most ε.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Algorithm 1's iterative price-signal coordination for the microgrid energy-sharing model. | Closed-loop iterative demand response within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Decentralized scheduling of PV prosumers during iterative energy sharing with demand response.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002"],"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","source_rule_sha256":"aa8f1f27d192643963a44e8fa99ed94cbde6970387ed22ac0c02463bcebd36c1"},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R003","market_meaning":"Organizing energy-sharing exchanges requires a coordinator, instantiated as the Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Scope: Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. The ESP coordinates energy-sharing activities and executes the local trading agency role by purchasing surplus electricity from PV prosumers and selling electricity to other prosumers. Scope: ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone. Local surplus-PV sharing is conditional on successful convergence of iterative price-signal coordination. In the successful branch the internal price is settled and prosumers agree to share; the failure branch leaves direct utility-grid trading available. Scope: Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. Condition: The iterative internal-price coordination process converges to a fixed point within Algorithm 1's iteration limit; k > K is the stated failure branch.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"activation","context_text":"ESP-mediated exchanges among PV prosumers in the energy-sharing zone. | Implementation of surplus-PV sharing through the distributed iterative process in Algorithm 1. | Organization of PV energy sharing in the proposed energy-sharing zone. | The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e16","v141-b-g01-e28","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g02-E-28","v141-b-g02-E-29"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003"],"decision_anchor":"execution.energy_trade","source_rule_sha256":"374605ad1b01a6db8884beca3c6b0faad6a333c662310321d595647cc6a10b0b"},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R006","market_meaning":"Updated requested net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h ≥ 0, which contribute to total buying power. Updated offered net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h \u003c 0, whose magnitudes contribute to total selling power. The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. Final internal prices are decided when the price-coordination process reaches a state in which no PV prosumer can adjust its schedule further. Scope: Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. Condition: After sufficient iterations, all PV prosumers can no longer adjust their schedules in response to the internal prices. The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1. Internal prices must remain between the feed-in tariff and the utility-grid electricity purchase price. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Internal-price design must guarantee the economic balance of the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. The internal selling price is Pr^{h}_{sell} = (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}). Scope: Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR^h ≤ 1. Both internal buying and selling prices equal the utility-grid export tariff. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. Condition: SDR > 1. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_sell^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h \u003c 0. The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_buy^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h ≥ 0.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"pricing","context_text":"Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. | Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices. | Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. | Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. | Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. | Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid. | Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. | Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26","v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E17","v141-b-g03-E18"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C011"],"decision_anchor":"pricing.local","source_rule_sha256":"56caf15ff85b7048a35707f2567847b37f3ebab30e4076668d222d792bbea136"},{"id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::V::pricing.local","rule_id":"v141-c-R008","market_meaning":"The ESP is responsible for assuring payment balance in the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. The ESP is responsible for charging participating prosumers a service fee for energy sharing. Scope: Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h. The service fee is directly proportional to the amount of shared local PV energy. Scope: The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. Each prosumer's service-fee share is allocated according to its contribution of shared local energy. Scope: Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. The service fee should cover sharing-power losses and other possible expenditures for organizing sharing activities. Scope: Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone.","omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Allocation of individual service-fee shares among participating PV prosumers. | Payment balance within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. | Service fees charged to participating PV prosumers for energy sharing. | Setting the service-fee level for the energy-sharing zone. | The ESP's aggregate service fee for PV energy sharing within the microgrid. | The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g01-e05","v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23","v141-b-g02-E-19","v141-b-g02-E-20","v141-b-g02-E-39"]},"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","source_rule_sha256":"fe990a393f5f5a128c4aeb63d22e38523e42ffec212540ef5888171d9331c382"}],"constraints":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R002-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Local internal prices provide the signal guiding each prosumer's scheduling decisions, with forecast PV power, load consumption and willingness taken into account. Scope: Decentralized scheduling of PV prosumers during iterative energy sharing with demand response.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R002::v141-c-R002-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R002","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal unit prices apply to the ESP's electricity purchases from and sales to PV prosumers. Scope: The prosumer-facing legs of ESP purchases and sales within the energy-sharing zone.","expression":"Pr_buy = unit price for ESP purchases of electricity from PV prosumers; Pr_sell = unit price for ESP sales of electricity to PV prosumers","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","execution.energy_trade"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R003-Pr_buy","v141-c-R003-Pr_sell"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e16","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"TSP h to SDRh = (7) TBP h th Considering the ﬂuctuation of PV power and users’ load, the λb SDR is a","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 3","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"As shown in Fig. 3, the ESP acts as an agent for all the PV prosumers. The ESP purchases power from PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_buy and \\lambda_{buy}, and sells power to PV prosumers and utility grid at the unit price of Pr_sell and \\lambda_{sell}, respectively."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Updated requested net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h ≥ 0, which contribute to total buying power.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C001","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"certain time slot based on the net power. Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power","equation_id":"(4)-(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power (TBP) at time slot h can be calculated as:\nTSP^{h} = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \u003c 0 \\quad (4)\nTBP^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \\geq 0 \\quad (5)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Updated offered net-energy quantities are sent to the ESP before it recalculates and broadcasts the internal prices. Scope: Successive scheduling iterations within the microgrid energy-sharing zone. Condition: For submitted net-power components with NP_i^h \u003c 0, whose magnitudes contribute to total selling power.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C002","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"certain time slot based on the net power. Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power","equation_id":"(4)-(5)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Thus, the Total Selling Power (TSP) and Total Buying Power (TBP) at time slot h can be calculated as:\nTSP^{h} = -\\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \u003c 0 \\quad (4)\nTBP^{h} = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} NP_{i}^{h}, \\quad NP_{i}^{h} \\geq 0 \\quad (5)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The ESP recalculates the internal prices. Scope: Internal-price updates during iterative energy sharing in one microgrid.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e03","v141-b-g02-E-26"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e03","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p03-c2r1__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":"3571","section":"II. ENERGY SHARING STRUCTURE OF PV PROSUMERS / B. Energy Sharing Structure","anchor_text":"NSE FOR MICROGRIDS OF PEER-TO-PEER PROSUMERS 3571 In order to facilitate the organization of energy ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In order to facilitate the organization of energy sharing, a coordinator is required. Here, we introduce a new entity named Energy Sharing Provider (ESP). Generally, the ESP may belong to the microgrid operator or an independent third party company that focuses on the business mode of energy sharing, which provides energy sharing service for all participated PV prosumers. The ESP acts as an agent for prosumers and is responsible for assuring the power balance and the payment balance in the energy sharing zone. In this regard, the ESP is in charge of purchasing electricity from the utility grid, or from the PV prosumers with extra net power export, then selling electricity to other prosumers or the utility grid."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C004","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Final internal prices are decided when the price-coordination process reaches a state in which no PV prosumer can adjust its schedule further. Scope: Finalization of internal prices in the closed-loop price-based demand-response process. Condition: After sufficient iterations, all PV prosumers can no longer adjust their schedules in response to the internal prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E-26"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E-26","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p07-c1r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"IV.B Iterative Algorithm","anchor_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is im","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"The interaction process for the energy sharing with DR is shown in Fig. 6. The overall process is implemented in a closed-loop iterative way. Optimal scheduling for each PV prosumer could be carried out according to the received internal price, considering the forecasting PV power, load consumption, and user's willingness. During the iterative optimization, the information exchange between the ESP and PV prosumers are listed in Table I.\nFor each step scheduling, PV prosumers' net power might be changed, and the new results will be sent to the ESP. Then the ESP recalculates and broadcasts the updated internal prices. After enough iterations, if all the PV prosumers can not adjust the scheduling anymore, the ﬁnal internal prices for PV energy sharing is decided."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C005","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The internal buying-price construction takes account of internal energy-sale costs, utility-grid charges and ESP charges. Scope: Construction of the internal buying price in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment","pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g03-E18"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"der When SDR = 0, which means no PV prosumer sells power, ded the required energy is bought from the","equation_id":"(10)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Secondly, the internal buying price is defined as an average value considering the cost of internal selling energy, utility grid's charge and the ESP's charge: Pr_{buy}^{h} = f(SDR^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h} \\cdot SDR^{h} + \\lambda_{buy}(1 - SDR^{h}), & 0 \\leq SDR^{h} \\leq 1 \\\\ \\lambda_{sell}, & SDR > 1 \\end{cases}   (10)  When 0 \u003c SDR^{h} \u003c 1, the total power demand exceeds the total power supply of PV systems in the energy sharing zone, the lacking power is bought from the utility grid at the price of \\lambda_{buy}."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C006","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal prices must remain between the feed-in tariff and the utility-grid electricity purchase price. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices in the microgrid energy-sharing zone.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal prices should be bounded between the feed-in tariff and electricity prices of utility grid; ii) as the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional; iii) the economic balance should always be guaranteed for the energy sharing zone."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C007","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Internal-price design must guarantee the economic balance of the energy-sharing zone. Scope: Design of the energy-sharing zone's internal prices.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e13","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":"3572","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / B. Internal Price Model","anchor_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal p","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Before designing energy sharing prices, we mainly consider three basic principles: i) the internal prices should be bounded between the feed-in tariff and electricity prices of utility grid; ii) as the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional; iii) the economic balance should always be guaranteed for the energy sharing zone."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C008","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The internal selling price is Pr^{h}_{sell} = (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}). Scope: Internal selling price at each time slot in the energy-sharing zone. Condition: 0 ≤ SDR^h ≤ 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E17"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E17","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":"(30)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function of internal selling price can be formulated as: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR^{h}) = { (λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^{h}+λ^{sell}), 0 ≤ SDR^{h} ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR^{h} > 1 } (30)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C009","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Both internal buying and selling prices equal the utility-grid export tariff. Scope: Internal buying and selling prices when the energy-sharing zone has surplus PV supply. Condition: SDR > 1.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E14","v141-b-g03-E18"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E14","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p11-c2r4__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":11,"printed_page":"3579","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"SDR. When SDR > 1, there must be extra PV energy export to the utility grid, then the selling price ","equation_id":"(27)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-11.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"According to the basic principle of economics, the relation between price and SDR is inverse-proportional. Thus, the price decrease with the higher SDR and increased with the lower SDR. When SDR > 1, there must be extra PV energy export to the utility grid, then the selling price could be set as λsell due to the constraints of feed-in tariff. When 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, as the sharing energy is lower than the load demand of the microgrid, the internal price can be set in accordance with the function of inverse proportion 1/(ax + b). Thus, we can use 1/(ax + b) as the fitting function to obtain the relationship between internal selling price and SDR: Pr^{h}_{sell} = f(SDR) = { 1/(aSDR+b), 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1 ; λ^{sell}, SDR > 1 } (27)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C010","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_sell^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h \u003c 0.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e23"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R006-C011","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer's applicable internal price is Pr_buy^h. Scope: Selection of the applicable internal price for prosumer i at time slot h. Condition: NP_i^h ≥ 0.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e23"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C011","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R006","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C003","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The applicable internal price enters the monetary electricity cost or income as the price multiplied by adjusted consumption minus PV production. Scope: The monetary electricity-cost or income component of a PV prosumer's net energy exchange at time slot h.","expression":"Pr_i^{h} \\left( x_i^{h} - P_i^{h} \\right)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e22","v141-b-g01-e23"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C003","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"h=1 where inci is the equivalent inconvenience cost of PV prosumer i, αi is the sensitivity coefﬁcie","equation_id":"(14),(15)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Integrating the inconvenience cost with the electricity cost or income of the PV prosumer, the cost function for optimal operation of PV prosumers can be defined as: C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) = Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) + \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}   (14) ; C_i = \\sum_{h=1}^{H} C_i^{h}(x_i^{h})   (15) where C_i^{h}(x_i^{h}) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Pr_i^{h}(x_i^{h} - P_i^{h}) and equivalent cost for adjusting flexible power \\alpha_i(x_i^{h} - TP_i^{h})^{2}. These two parts constitute the cost function in both economy and users' willingness."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"3573","section":"III. ENERGY SHARING MODEL / C. Cost Model of the PV Prosumer","anchor_text":"where Chi (xhi ) can be separated into two parts: cost for using electricity Prhi (xhi −P ih ) and e","equation_id":"(16)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Pr_i^{h} is the price at time slot h for prosumer i, which can be selling price or buying price, and decided by the net power: Pr_i^{h} = f(NP_i^{h}) = \\begin{cases} Pr_{sell}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \u003c 0 \\\\ Pr_{buy}^{h}, & NP_i^{h} \\geq 0 \\end{cases}   (16)"}]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R008-C007","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"For 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, the energy-sharing zone's economic-balance condition equates total buying payments with internal selling receipts plus the ESP's utility-grid purchase cost of the residual: TBP·Pr_buy = TSP·Pr_sell + (TBP−TSP)λ^buy.","expression":"TBP \\cdot Pr_{buy} = TSP \\cdot Pr_{sell} + (TBP - TSP)\\lambda^{buy}, \\quad 0 \\leq SDR \\leq 1","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g04-e04","v141-b-g03-E18"],"ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007","source_rule_id":"v141-c-R008","evidence":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g04-e04","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"a = λbλbuuy y−λsλs e ellll (29) b = λb1u y w Finally, by substituting (29) into (28), the function o","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"(31) TBP\\cdot Pr_{buy}=TSP\\cdot Pr_{sell}+(TBP-TSP)\\lambda^{buy}"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E18","location":{"location_id":"src-0812c00672-p12-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":12,"printed_page":"3580","section":"Appendix I","anchor_text":"TBP · Prbuy = TSP · Prsell + (TBP TSP) λ (31) By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Prbuy =","equation_id":"(31), (32), (33), (34)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-12.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Considering the economical balance requirement of the energy sharing zone, we can further deduce the internal buying price Pr^{h}_{buy} based on the internal selling price Pr^{h}_{sell}. If 0 ≤ SDR ≤ 1, since the ESP need to purchase energy from the utility grid, the economic balance can be described as: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TSP · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TSP) λ^{buy} (31). By substituting (7) into (31), there is: TBP · Pr_{buy} = TBP · SDR · Pr_{sell} + (TBP − TBP · SDR) λ^{buy} (32). Thus, we can deduce the Pr_{buy} as: Pr_{buy} = SDR · Pr_{sell} + (1 − SDR) λ^{buy} (33). Otherwise, if SDR > 1, similar with the condition of internal selling price, the internal buying price is: Pr_{buy} = λ^{sell} (34)."}]}],"variables":[],"parameters":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-Pr_buy","symbol":"Pr_buy","meaning":"Internal buying price of the energy-sharing zone; unit price at which the ESP purchases electricity from PV prosumers on the prosumer-facing leg of energy-trade execution.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-Pr_buy"},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R003-Pr_sell","symbol":"Pr_sell","meaning":"Internal selling price of the energy-sharing zone; unit price at which the ESP sells electricity to PV prosumers on the prosumer-facing leg of energy-trade execution.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e16"],"source_rule_id":"v141-c-R003","declaration_ref":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::theta::v141-c-R003-Pr_sell"}]}],"source_definitions":[{"unit_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-a-M01::pricing.local","stage":"L6","subtype":"internal_tariff_formation_and_application","projection_status":"composite","target_definition":"Contains SDR internal electricity price formation and transaction-side applicable definitions. The pricing constraint specifies: when 0≤SDR^h≤1, Pr_sell^h=(λ^{sell}·λ^{buy})/((λ^{buy}−λ^{sell})·SDR^h+λ^{sell}), Pr_buy^h=SDR^h·Pr_sell^h+(1−SDR^h)λ^{buy}; when SDR^h>1, both prices are λ^{sell}. When prosumer NP_i^h\u003c0, Pr_sell^h applies; when NP_i^h≥0, Pr_buy^h applies. At trade execution, Pr_buy and Pr_sell are separately defined as the ESP electricity purchase and sale unit prices, respectively; this independent transaction-side specification must be retained.","form_kind":"mathematical","identity_fields":["Object: the internal unit electricity price of the sharing area and the applicable transaction side","Core operation: form electricity prices by SDR segments and select the applicable price according to the sign of the prosumer's net quantity","Output: Pr_sell^h, Pr_buy^h, and Pr_i^h","Independent definition: Pr_buy and Pr_sell, named at the execution point according to the ESP purchase/sale direction"],"variation_fields":["The electricity price boundaries are the feed-in tariff and the grid purchase price.","After receiving the updated net quantity, ESP recalculates the price; when dispatch no longer changes, the final price is determined.","When 0≤SDR≤1, retain the revenue-expenditure constraint TBP·Pr_buy=TSP·Pr_sell+(TBP−TSP)λ^{buy}.","The buying-price formula retains the original formula; no service-fee term is added additionally because of the textual description of the fee composition.","The ESP-side naming and the buy/sell directions of the prosumer net-quantity branch are retained separately."],"constraint_refs":["06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R003::v141-c-R003-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C003","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C004","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C005","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C006","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C008","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C009","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C010","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R006::v141-c-R006-C011","06-sdr_energy_sharing::v141-c-R008::v141-c-R008-C007"],"paper_id":"06-sdr_energy_sharing","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","function":"pricing.local","template_code":"PGR"}],"source_variants":[],"functional":{"is_child":false,"subdivision_pending":false},"canonical_pointer":"/nodes/29"});
